{# The agent-drafted survey report — the v2 document, with a model-written
   narrative in place of the deterministic prose.

   Session V2-WIRE (WIRING.md slice W5). This mirrors, exactly, what the
   markdown path has always done: the model drafts PROSE, and the evidence layer
   is rendered deterministically from the same AnalysisResult and spliced around
   it. `drafted_evidence.md.j2` is that splice for markdown; this is it for the
   v2 page, and both use the same suppression flags, computed in the same place
   (`generate.py::_drafted_evidence_block`'s caller).

   WHAT IS DETERMINISTIC HERE, and it is the point:

     * the masthead, the status line, the GATE RIBBON, the meta strip, the
       webapp's notes, and the severity/diagnosis card pair;
     * the analysis parameters, the damage stage, the spectral figures, the
       cause hypotheses with their illustrations and every citation;
     * the provenance panel, the blank signature rules and the footer.

   The model writes the narrative between them and nothing else. In particular
   the gate ribbon is deterministic on THIS path too, so every non-PASS check
   still reaches the reader verbatim, above the diagnosis, on a document whose
   prose a language model wrote.

   Sections the draft already carries are suppressed rather than duplicated —
   `want_parameters`, `want_causes`, `want_signature` — which is the same rule,
   and the same flags, the markdown appendix has used since Session H.

   The appendix headings carry NO section numbers here. The narrative supplies
   the document's structure and its own headings are unnumbered, so a numbered
   appendix restarting at 1 underneath them read as a second document rather
   than as the end of this one. #}
{% import "_v2.html.j2" as v2 %}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>Vibration Survey Report — {{ machine.name }}</title>
<style>{{ stylesheet }}</style>
</head>
<body>
<main class="doc">

{{ v2.masthead(machine) }}
{{ v2.status_banner(status_line, status_colour) }}
{{ v2.gate_ribbon(gate, dq_notes) }}
{{ v2.notes_panel(notes) }}

{# ── PAGE 1 · the fault sheet ──────────────────────────────────────────────
   DETERMINISTIC on the drafted path too, and the same macro the deterministic
   page renders: it carries the health line, the fault, the decision, the
   recommendation in its three parts and the escalation trigger, none of which
   the model authors. The model's narrative starts on page 2 with the rest of
   the Evidence. #}
{{ v2.fault_sheet(fault_sheet, charts, sheet_figure) }}

<h2 class="evidence-head">Evidence</h2>
{{ v2.meta_strip(machine, result, analysis_parameters) }}
{{ v2.cards(ctx) }}

{# ── the drafted narrative ────────────────────────────────────────────────
   The model's own markdown, converted. Its headings become the document's
   prose headings; every number in it has already been re-checked against the
   computed result, and a draft that failed any of those checks never reaches
   this template — the job degrades to the deterministic report instead. #}
<section class="narrative">
{{ narrative }}
</section>

{% if want_parameters %}
{{ v2.parameters_section(none, machine_rows, analysis_parameters) }}
{% endif %}

{# Session REPORT-2: no want_* flag — the reference report the model is handed
   omits the Fmax-adequacy block, so there is no draft copy to suppress.
   Rendered deterministically on every drafted page. #}
{{ v2.fmax_adequacy_section(none, fmax_adequacy) }}

{# Session REC-1 — the HTML twin of drafted_evidence.md.j2's call. Suppressed
   when the draft wrote its own Recommendations heading, exactly as want_stage
   suppresses the damage-stage block. #}
{% if want_recommendations %}
{{ v2.recommendations_section(none, recommendations) }}
{% endif %}

{# Session REPORT-3 (item 4) — PARTC F-10's other half, byte-for-byte guarded.
   See drafted_evidence.md.j2 for why the probe is the order COLUMNS and not
   the "Evidence" heading. #}
{% if want_evidence_table %}
{{ v2.evidence_table(none, evidence_rows) }}
{% endif %}

{% if want_stage %}
{{ v2.damage_stage_section(none, damage_stage, stage_graphic) }}
{% elif stage_graphic %}
{# The draft wrote its own damage-stage prose, so rendering the deterministic
   block too would put a second section under the same heading — which is what a
   shipped sample did. The LADDER is not a duplicate of that prose: it is the
   only place the reading's position on the product's own three-rung scale is
   drawn, and its caption explains itself. So it renders alone. #}
<section>{{ stage_graphic }}</section>
{% endif %}

{% if charts and charts.trend %}
<section>
  <h2>Trend chart</h2>
  <figure><div class="plot"><img src="{{ charts.trend.rel_path }}" alt="{{ charts.trend.alt }}"></div></figure>
</section>
{% endif %}

{# Session HIST-1: no want_* flag, for the REPORT-NA reason — the reference
   report the model is handed says the history was analyst-supplied, but a
   caveat about the EVIDENCE is not the model's to write or to omit, so it is
   spliced deterministically. Guarded on the provenance rather than on the
   chart: the claim is about the data, not about the picture of it, and a render
   with figures off must still carry it. #}
{% if history_provenance %}
<section>
  {{ v2.history_provenance_note(history_provenance, custom_basis) }}
</section>
{% endif %}

{{ v2.spectral_section(none, charts) }}

{# Session HIST-2: no want_* flag, for the REPORT-NA reason — the reference
   report the model is handed omits the comparison entirely, so there is no
   draft copy to suppress and no delta the model could have narrated. #}
{{ v2.comparison_section(none, comparison) }}

{{ v2.causes_section(none, causes if want_causes else none, cause_heading, cause_illustration) }}

{# Session REPORT-NA: no want_* flag — the reference report the model is handed
   omits the coverage roster, so there is no draft copy to suppress. Rendered
   deterministically on every drafted page. #}
{{ v2.coverage_section(none, coverage) }}

{{ v2.provenance_panel() }}
{% if want_signature %}
{{ v2.signature_block() }}
{% endif %}
{{ v2.page_footer(deletion_footer) }}

</main>
</body>
</html>
